{{!-- The Inventar tab: the three administrative lists.

This is deliberately *not* a second slot-budget view. The Basics tab answers
"what am I wearing" and "what counts against my budget" — questions asked
mid-roll. This tab is the complete ledger behind them: every object the
character owns appears here exactly once, whatever state it is in. Creating,
editing and deleting live here for the same reason.

Features and Active Effects follow it because they are the other two things an
actor owns that are not objects — they cost no slots, so they can never appear
in the slot raster, and before this tab existed they had nowhere to be. --}}

{{!-- ------------------------------------------------------------------
Gear, grouped by the role each piece carries. Roles are mutually exclusive, so
every object still appears exactly once — the groups are a reading of the one
list rather than four lists that could disagree.

Which columns stand between the name and the controls is the reader's choice
(see the column picker), so the table is built as a single CSS grid whose track
list comes from the context: one grid for the whole thing, not one per group,
because that is what keeps every group's columns lined up under one header. --}}
<div class='basics-section-header item-table-header'>
  <h3 class='basics-section-title'>{{localize 'TNO.Inventory.CarrySlots'}}</h3>
  <input type='text' class='item-search-input' value='{{itemTable.search}}'
         placeholder='{{localize "TNO.ItemTable.Search"}}'
         title='{{localize "TNO.ItemTable.SearchHint"}}' />
  <a class='item-columns-toggle' title='{{localize "TNO.ItemTable.ColumnsHint"}}'>
    <i class='fas fa-table-columns'></i>{{localize 'TNO.ItemTable.Columns'}}
  </a>
  {{#if editable}}
    {{!-- `.section-add` is the look, `.inventory-add` is the action — the two
    are separate classes so the Merkmale button below can wear the same control
    without also triggering the gear-authoring dialog this one opens. --}}
    <a class='section-add inventory-add' title='{{localize "TNO.Inventory.AddHint"}}'>
      <i class='fas fa-plus'></i>
    </a>
  {{/if}}
</div>

{{#if itemTable.empty}}
  <p class='items-empty'>{{localize 'TNO.Inventory.Empty'}}</p>
{{else}}
  <div class='item-table-scroll'>
    <div class='item-table' style='grid-template-columns: {{itemTable.gridTemplate}};'>

      {{!-- One header row for the whole table. Each caption sorts the table by
      its column; the sort is view-only and never rewrites `item.sort`, which is
      what the Basics slot bands pack from. --}}
      <div class='item-thead'>
        {{#each itemTable.headers as |column|}}
          <a class='item-th item-table-sort{{#if column.numeric}} numeric{{/if}}{{#if column.sorted}} sorted{{/if}}'
             data-sort-key='{{column.key}}'
             title='{{column.hint}} — {{column.sortHint}}'>
            <span class='item-th-label'>{{column.label}}</span>
            {{#if column.sorted}}
              <i class='fas {{#ifEquals column.dir "desc"}}fa-caret-down{{else}}fa-caret-up{{/ifEquals}}'
                 aria-hidden='true'></i>
            {{/if}}
          </a>
        {{/each}}
        <div class='item-th item-th-controls'></div>
      </div>

      {{#each itemTable.groups as |group|}}
        {{!-- Every group renders even when it holds nothing, so the table keeps
        its shape as items come and go and a missing heading never has to be
        read as "that group is gone" rather than "none of those". --}}
        <div class='item-group' data-group='{{group.role}}'>
          <span class='item-group-name'>{{group.label}}</span>
          <span class='xp-badge' title='{{group.badgeHint}}'>{{group.badge}}</span>
        </div>

        {{#if group.rows.length}}
          {{#each group.rows as |row|}}
            {{!-- `draggable` so a piece can still be dragged out of the ledger
            onto the hotbar or another actor. Dropping one *back* onto the table
            sorts nothing — see `_onSortItem`. --}}
            <div class='item-row draggable{{#if row.worn}} is-worn{{/if}}'
                 data-item-id='{{row.id}}' data-group='{{group.role}}'
                 data-name='{{row.name}}' draggable='true'>
              <div class='item-td item-td-name'>
                {{!-- The role icon rather than the artwork, matching the carry
                grid: a repeated, recognisable glyph is quicker to scan down a
                list than ninety different portraits. --}}
                {{#if row.img}}
                  <img class='inventory-item-icon slot-art' src='{{row.img}}' alt='' />
                {{else}}
                  <i class='fa-solid {{row.icon}} inventory-item-icon' aria-hidden='true'></i>
                {{/if}}
                <span class='item-row-name' title='{{row.name}}'>{{row.name}}</span>
              </div>

              {{#each row.cells as |cell|}}
                <div class='item-td{{#if cell.numeric}} numeric{{/if}}{{#if cell.na}} is-na{{/if}}{{#if cell.blank}} is-blank{{/if}}{{#if cell.warn}} is-warn{{/if}}'
                     title='{{cell.title}}'>{{cell.text}}</div>
              {{/each}}

              <div class='item-td item-controls'>
                {{#if row.worn}}
                  {{!-- A marker, not a control: taking a piece off belongs to
                  the paper doll, which is the only view that knows which zones
                  it occupies. --}}
                  <span class='item-state' title='{{localize "TNO.Inventory.WornHint"}}'>
                    <i class='fas fa-shield-halved'></i>
                  </span>
                {{/if}}
                <a class='item-control item-edit' title='{{localize "TNO.Item.Edit"}}'>
                  <i class='fas fa-edit'></i>
                </a>
                {{!-- `@root.editable`, not `editable`: inside an `each` a bare
                name resolves against the row, which has no such key, so the
                whole block silently vanished. --}}
                {{#if @root.editable}}
                  {{#unless row.worn}}
                    <a class='item-control item-delete' title='{{localize "TNO.Item.Delete"}}'>
                      <i class='fas fa-trash'></i>
                    </a>
                  {{else}}
                    {{!-- Held back rather than hidden, so the row keeps its
                    shape and says why: `system.equipment` addresses the piece
                    by id, and deleting it out from under the doll would strand
                    a zone. --}}
                    <span class='item-control is-disabled' title='{{localize "TNO.Item.DeleteWornHint"}}'>
                      <i class='fas fa-trash'></i>
                    </span>
                  {{/unless}}
                {{/if}}
              </div>
            </div>
          {{/each}}
        {{else}}
          <p class='item-group-empty' data-group='{{group.role}}'>{{localize 'TNO.ItemTable.GroupEmpty'}}</p>
        {{/if}}
      {{/each}}

    </div>
    <p class='item-table-nomatch' hidden>{{localize 'TNO.ItemTable.NoMatch'}}</p>
  </div>
{{/if}}

{{> "systems/tno/templates/actor/parts/actor-features.hbs"}}

{{!-- ------------------------------------------------------------------
Active Effects. Foundry's own mechanic rather than one of this system's, but
an effect applied to the character was previously visible nowhere on the
sheet at all. --}}
<div class='basics-section-header'>
  <h3 class='basics-section-title'>{{localize 'TNO.TabEffects'}}</h3>
</div>
